# Lizard Man of Lagarto

## Lore

Reptilian humanoids of the rivers, swamps and lakes of Lagarto, with fine green scales, bright green or blue eyes, a spiny crest down the tail and a mouth full of small sharp teeth. Over the last fifteen years their people have split in two. The traditional lizard men remain reclusive, primitive hunters. The rest follow New Dragcona and the cult of Dragonwright, and have become the militant, technologically sophisticated soldiers of the "Nation of Scaled Peoples", many of them recruited young and drilled in methods borrowed from the Coalition States and Atlantis.

Some of those trained soldiers have deserted, joining the resistance or selling their skills abroad as mercenaries and pirates. A player character can come from either group.

## GM Notes

A traditional lizard man knows little of technology, and the choice of occupation should reflect that. A Lagarto soldier or deserter is best played as a Headhunter, Wilderness Scout or Special Forces soldier, and takes the Soldier of Lagarto ability. Lagarto''s army is equipped mostly with Kittani gear - explorer armour, a sword and a pulse rifle for the rank and file, and light power armour for elite units - while rebels rely on ancient weapons and techno-wizard equipment.
', 'published', 'data-script'
